{"type":"bullets","design":"ENGINE_BULLETS","title":"Enterprise compliance and privacy boundaries","lead":"Enforcing strict data sovereignty, tenant isolation, and governance controls across Google Cloud.","points":["Zero customer data training: Catalog data, pricing logic, and shopper queries remain isolated and are never used to train foundation models.","VPC Service Controls: Perimeter security restricts data movement across BigQuery, Cloud Storage, and Vertex AI to prevent exfiltration.","Customer-managed encryption: Cloud KMS keys secure data at rest and in transit for clickstream logs, Pro accounts, and merchandising tables.","PII redaction pipelines: Cloud Data Loss Prevention masks payment details, addresses, and identifiers before events reach model indexes.","IAM least-privilege governance: Granular role-based policies separate merchandising, data engineering, and security administration across environments."],"callout":{"label":"Sovereign AI governance","title":"Grounding models strictly in verified enterprise data","text":"Gemini and Vertex AI Search ground every response in Home Depot's governed BigQuery catalog and policy documents, operating within an isolated Google Cloud tenant with enterprise-grade compliance and sovereignty controls."},"notes":"Enterprise AI deployment requires strict data isolation and governance boundaries. All catalog attributes, Pro customer lists, and clickstream signals remain within Home Depot's isolated Google Cloud project boundary protected by VPC Service Controls and customer-managed encryption keys. Gemini and Vertex AI Search ground responses strictly in the client's own content without training underlying foundation models on proprietary retail data.

