{"type":"cards","design":"S66_ISSUE_ROWS","title":"Key risks and how we mitigate them","lead":"Proactive engineering controls neutralize cutover, latency, schema, and compliance risks.","items":[{"title":"Ledger drift during database cutover","fix":"Stream continuous changes using Database Migration Service; Run automated row-hash reconciliation scripts prior to cutover; Halt legacy writes briefly before promoting AlloyDB primary; Validate data integrity across clusters before enabling active traffic.","status":"warning","icon":"database"},{"title":"Cross-region query latency spikes","fix":"Deploy local AlloyDB read pools in both regions; Route balance verification queries to local regional instances; Configure Cloud Run to prefer regional database endpoints; Ensure cross-zone latency stays minimized for real-time customer lookups.","status":"warning","icon":"analytics"},{"title":"Downstream gateway timeouts under burst","fix":"Enforce strict concurrency limits on Cloud Run services; Implement circuit breakers for external payment gateway calls; Buffer failed settlement messages in Pub/Sub dead-letter queues; Isolate cascading failures to protect underlying core transactional nodes.","status":"warning","icon":"security"}],"notes":"We mitigate the four primary technical risks before production traffic shifts. Database Migration Service validation prevents ledger drift, regional AlloyDB read pools eliminate cross-region read latency, and automated policy checks enforce Cloud KMS and IAM boundaries.

